From 71d6d7a2cdc4d74771b51e33a401794494cf0854 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ashhart <71890694+ashhart@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 15:23:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] rows: try one shorter disk state after a refused read
 (backport #2442)

Backported from 12d61cb6b96c968aab76b8c53444380e66a76f53 to f350cd3e with recipe patches 0001-0112. Retains the two-tier GLM snapshot budget checks from 0109 and registers the original fallback tests through rows_store.zig on this pin.

Integration note: now numbered 0122 after main renumbered 0107-0117 to 0111-0121. The two-tier checks originally in 0109 are now in 0113; the diff below is unchanged.

The pinned recipe retains a valid RAM state when a disk restore fails. Preserve that behavior after both bounded disk attempts as well, with an additional regression covering two damaged disk states beside a valid shorter RAM state. Name the actual terminal fallback in the log.
---
